      "title": "Mapping the Frame: Questioning Your Problem Architecture",
      "prompt": "We often mistake the trigger of a decision for the actual problem. Think of an urgent decision currently on your desk. Strip away the initial alarm bells: what is the fundamental choice hidden underneath? How does reframing this trigger from a restrictive binary ('Should I do X or Y?') into an expansive inquiry ('What ultimate outcome am I engineering?') alter the possibilities?",
      "placeholder": "Deconstruct the trigger vs. the real underlying problem..."
