      "title": "Objective Deconstruction: Uncovering Fundamental Drivers",
      "prompt": "Our minds frequently confuse 'means' (the vehicles we take) with 'ends' (where we actually want to arrive). Take your core goal for this quarter and repeatedly ask 'Why is that important?' until you hit bedrock. Which of your stated objectives are merely operational stepping stones, and which are pure, non-negotiable values?",
      "placeholder": "Trace each objective back to its fundamental root..."
