      "title": "Even Swap Diagnostic: Finding Your Real Currency of Value",
      "prompt": "Trade-offs feel agonizing because we try to compare apples to gravity. Isolate two competing alternatives that clash on different criteria (e.g., higher salary vs. shorter commute). How much compensation would precisely balance losing two hours of daily freedom? What does your break-even point reveal about your true hierarchy of values?",
