      "chapterOrder": 6,
      "title": "Uncertainty Autopsy: Separating Odds from Outcomes",
      "prompt": "Human psychology naturally conflates a bad outcome with a bad decision. Dissect a past gamble that soured: was the process flawed, or was it a mathematically sound bet hit by low-probability turbulence? How can you decouple your self-worth from sheer statistical variance?",
      "placeholder": "Analyze the decision quality independent of how luck played out..."
